,552,555,558,561,564,567],{"id":496,"title":497},"howto.get-started","Get started — a first project",{"id":499,"title":500},"howto.first-drum-beat","Program a first drum beat",{"id":502,"title":503},"howto.first-bassline","Record a bassline live",{"id":505,"title":506},"howto.first-chords","Add chords on steps",{"id":508,"title":509},"howto.first-punch-in","Perform with punch-in FX",{"id":511,"title":512},"howto.enable-velocity","Make the keyboard velocity-sensitive",{"id":514,"title":515},"howto.control-synth-midi","Play an external synth over MIDI",{"id":517,"title":518},"howto.control-cv-synth","Play an analog synth with CV and gate",{"id":520,"title":521},"howto.sync-drum-machine","Sync a vintage drum machine",{"id":523,"title":524},"howto.sync-pocket-operator","Sync a pocket operator",{"id":526,"title":527},"howto.external-effect","Loop an external effect pedal",{"id":529,"title":530},"howto.midi-keyboard","Play the OP-XY from a MIDI keyboard",{"id":532,"title":533},"howto.audio-interface","Use an audio interface with the OP-XY",{"id":535,"title":536},"howto.pitchbend-modulation","Use the pitchbend strip as a modulator",{"id":538,"title":539},"howto.back-up-projects","Back up projects to a computer",{"id":541,"title":542},"howto.load-samples","Load samples from a computer",{"id":544,"title":545},"howto.song-with-brain","Sketch a song fast with the brain",{"id":547,"title":548},"howto.song-from-scenes","Build a song from scenes",{"id":550,"title":551},"howto.loop-one-scene","Loop one scene",{"id":553,"title":554},"howto.sidechain-duck","Make a track pump with the kick (duck)",{"id":556,"title":557},"howto.pluck","Turn a sound into a pluck",{"id":559,"title":560},"howto.pad-swell","A pad that swells in and fades slowly",{"id":562,"title":563},"howto.wobble","A filter wobble in time with the beat",{"id":565,"title":566},"howto.acid-bass","A squelchy acid bass",{"id":568,"title":569},"howto.slice-a-loop","Sample a loop and play it in slices"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":177,"prev":179,"next":181,"titles":183,"firmware":352},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":11,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":26,"procedures":103,"parameters":127,"related":146,"body":154,"sources":155,"official_url":30,"controls":169},"sampler.sampling","Sampling with the sample key",[5,6,7,8,9,10],"record a sample","sample key","sample mode","sampling threshold","record page","arm the recorder","sampler",10,"knowledge/manual/units/sampler/sampling.md",{"modes":15,"screens":16},[],[17],"sample","`sample` opens a record page from any screen: set source, gain and threshold, then arm the recorder — `hold M1` on the library page, a key and then `hold M1` on the drum sampler and multisampler, a keyboard key on the synth sampler. The take starts once the input passes the threshold.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":24,"verified_on":25},"1.0.9",[23],"1.0.29","1.1.15",null,[27,32,35,38,41,45,49,52,56,59,63,66,69,73,77,81,86,91,94,97,100],{"id":28,"text":29,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"which-page","On a sampler track, `sample` opens that engine's record page; on other tracks it records a stand-alone sample for the library.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#arrange","official",{"id":33,"text":34,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"limit","A sample can be at most 20 seconds long, in every sampler.",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"arm","On the library record page (a track without a sampler engine), holding `M1` arms the recorder.",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"threshold","Every record page has a threshold on `E4`, the level at which recording begins, so arming alone does not start the take; it starts when the input rises past that level.",{"id":42,"text":43,"source":44,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"arm-keyed","On the drum sampler and multisampler record pages you first press the keyboard key the take should go to (it lights up), then `hold M1`.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#drum-sampler",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":48,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"arm-synth","The synth sampler's record page starts sampling from a keyboard key, which also becomes the sample's root note; the guide gives that page no `M1` gesture.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/sample#one-shot-synth-sampler",{"id":50,"text":51,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"end","The guide does not say what ends a take before the 20-second limit, such as whether letting go of `M1` stops it; not yet checked on a unit.",{"id":53,"text":54,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":55},"meter","The level meter previews the input while you set the gain, and TE's pictures draw the threshold as an orange line across it.","derived",{"id":57,"text":58,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"keep-or-bin","On the library record page, `M2` plays the take back and `M4` deletes it before it reaches the library.",{"id":60,"text":61,"source":62,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":55},"where","A stand-alone take should land in the library's user folder (samples → user over MTP). The sample chapter says only that it goes to the library, but TE's load-samples how-to names user as the folder for samples recorded on the unit; not yet checked on a unit.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#how-to-load-samples",{"id":64,"text":65,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"exit","Pressing the lit track key closes the record page.",{"id":67,"text":68,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"sources","The sources TE documents for the sample page are the built-in mic, line in and USB; the guide names line in and USB as the ones with an input channel and draws the page with the mic selected. Tutorial videos on OS 1.0.x show a longer list, see the record-sources fact.",{"id":70,"text":71,"source":72,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":55},"not-t5-inputs","The guide never offers headset on the sample page and lists it among the external audio track's inputs (`T5`); tutorial videos do show a headset mic on the record page, see the record-sources fact.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/auxiliary#external-audio",{"id":74,"text":75,"source":76,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"mic","The built-in microphone can be the source, so sampling needs no cable.","https://teenage.engineering/products/op-xy",{"id":78,"text":79,"source":80,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"channel-since","Picking the input channel for line in and USB arrived in OS 1.0.29.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy#1.0.28",{"id":82,"text":83,"source":84,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":85},"channel-conflict","TE's audio-interface how-to picks the USB channel with `turn E2` instead; not yet checked on a unit.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#use-an-audio-interface-with-op-xy","conflicting",{"id":87,"text":88,"source":89,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":90},"record-sources","The record page's sources run mic, headset mic, line in and then resample last (a tutorial video on OS 1.0.x; the page's USB entry was not seen in that list).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":92,"text":93,"source":89,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":90},"gain-range","The record page's gain runs up to +31, and the screen prints the lowest and middle settings as +0 (two videos, OS 1.0.x).",{"id":95,"text":96,"source":89,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":90},"channel-letters","Beside the source icon the page shows the letters L and R for the input channel; shift + E1 changes which is lit (one video, OS 1.0.x).",{"id":98,"text":99,"source":89,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":90},"resample-silent","Resample records what the unit itself plays, so the meter stays silent until the transport is running (one video, OS 1.0.x).",{"id":101,"text":102,"source":89,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":90},"take-names","A take is named project, note, track and .wav joined by hyphens, in lower case, for example unnamed-f2-5.wav (three videos). The note uses C3 = 60 and the track counts from 1. A stand-alone library take uses F2 and the current track, a drum or multisampler take uses its key's note, and a synth sampler take uses its root note.",[104],{"id":105,"goal":106,"preconditions":107,"steps":109,"result":126,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"record","Record a sample into the library",[108],"the selected track does not use a sampler engine",[110,111,114,117,120,123],{"keys":17,"note":25,"set":25},{"keys":112,"note":113,"set":25},"turn E1","the source; `shift + turn E1` picks the channel of line in or USB",{"keys":115,"note":116,"set":25},"turn E3","the gain, watching the level meter",{"keys":118,"note":119,"set":25},"turn E4","the threshold, just above the room's noise",{"keys":121,"note":122,"set":25},"hold M1","arms the recorder; the take starts when the sound passes the threshold",{"keys":124,"note":125,"set":25},"M2","listen back; `M4` throws the take away instead","The take is saved to the library (by TE's how-to, in its user folder) unless you press `M4`.",[128,134,139,143],{"screen":17,"encoder":129,"layer":130,"keys":112,"name":131,"range":132,"default":25,"cc":25,"cc_confidence":25,"note":133,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E1","base","source","mic / headset mic / line in / resample","the order seen in tutorial videos, with resample last; TE's guide documents mic, line in and USB",{"screen":17,"encoder":129,"layer":135,"keys":136,"name":137,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":25,"cc_confidence":25,"note":138,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"shift","shift + turn E1","input channel","line in and USB only",{"screen":17,"encoder":140,"layer":130,"keys":115,"name":141,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":25,"cc_confidence":25,"note":142,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E3","gain","shown on the meter",{"screen":17,"encoder":144,"layer":130,"keys":118,"name":39,"range":25,"default":25,"cc":25,"cc_confidence":25,"note":145,"source":30,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":25,"confidence":31},"E4","the input level at which an armed recorder starts the take",[147,148,149,150,151,152,153],"sampler.overview","sampler.synth-sampler","sampler.drum-sampler","sampler.multisampler","sampler.sample-files","sampler.sample-library","auxiliary.external-audio","Every record page runs in the same order: choose the source, set the gain against the meter, put\nthe threshold just above the room noise, then arm. Arming only readies the recorder; the take\nbegins with the first sound that passes the threshold, so it starts on the note rather than on\nsilence. Each engine's unit has its own key handling.",[156,158,159,160,161,162,164,166,167],{"url":30,"kind":157},"guide",{"url":44,"kind":157},{"url":48,"kind":157},{"url":62,"kind":157},{"url":72,"kind":157},{"url":76,"kind":163},"te",{"url":80,"kind":165},"changelog",{"url":84,"kind":157},{"url":89,"kind":168},"research",[170,171,172,173,174,175,176],"key.sample","encoder.1","encoder.3","encoder.4","key.m1","key.m2","key.shift",{"id":11,"title":178},"Sampler",{"id":147,"title":180},"Samplers at a glance",{"id":148,"title":182},"Synth sampler",{"basics.key-notation":184,"basics.main-modes":185,"basics.modules":186,"basics.track-buttons":187,"basics.linked-tracks":188,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":189,"basics.workflow":190,"basics.firmware-versions":191,"hardware.layout":192,"hardware.power-and-charging":193,"hardware.connectors":194,"hardwar